# Arrakis Control Dashboard Engineering Rules

## 1. System & Architecture Constraints
- The project is migrating to a Next.js App Router workspace located inside `src/dashboard/src/app/`.
- Core domain layer relies on a `DuneConsoleClient` instance for querying character stats, level progress, Intel, Solaris Coins, credits, scrip, health, hydration, spice-addiction indicators, and base infrastructure.
- Never write or use third-party server frameworks like Express; strictly use native core Next.js Route Handlers.

## 2. Anti-Model-Laziness Protocols
- CRITICAL: You must write out the complete body blocks for all requested JavaScript functions, layout pages, and dynamic API responses.
- NEVER truncate logic strings or use placeholder comments (e.g., "// implementation here", "// rest of code remains unchanged").

## 3. Tool-Calling Stability & Optimization
- Always invoke exactly ONE tool call at a time. Never chain or stack multiple file modifications into a single prompt iteration block.
- Keep all conversational filler or explanations minimal; prioritize immediate and accurate file modifications.

## 4. Absolute File Path Integrity & Target Directory Boundaries
- CRITICAL SCOPE BOUNDARY: You are ONLY allowed to work inside the Next.js App Router tree. 
- Every automated tool invocation targeting file creation MUST start exactly with: `src/dashboard/src/app/`
- The true absolute directory anchor on this machine is: `C:\Users\RealXKenny\Documents\GitHub\Arrakis-Control\src\dashboard\src\`
- NEVER combine folders with dot suffixes (do NOT use `src/dashboard.src/app/`). It MUST be written as a clean directory slash structure: `src/dashboard/src/app/`.